      trivia: "【A Cigar Whose Name Changes at the Border】The same Honduran-made contents have been sold as 'Hoyo de Monterrey Excalibur' in the United States and simply as 'Excalibur' in Germany and Britain. Dan Blumenthal, chairman of Villazon, stated: 'We cannot use the Hoyo de Monterrey name, so we developed the Excalibur brand and sell it in Germany and England. In America, Excalibur is a line extension of Hoyo de Monterrey.'\n【A Blend Decided by Consumers】The sub-line '1066' is explained as having been created when General Cigar sent two trial blends to devotees, asked their preference, and produced the winner. The name is the year of the Battle of Hastings, and the formats — Lancelot, Merlin, King Arthur — are unified under the Arthurian theme.\n【To Nicaragua for the First Time in Its Fortieth Year】Following the 40th anniversary in 2021, 'The Illusione of Excalibur' — the brand's first outside collaboration — was a joint work between Dion Giolito of Illusione and Justin Andrews of General Cigar, made at the Aganorsa Leaf factory in Estelí. It became the first cigar of the Honduran-born Excalibur ever rolled in Nicaragua."
