      trivia: "'2012 by Oscar', the wellspring of Leaf by Oscar, was conceived in the year 2012, reckoned a threshold in the Mayan calendar. Each box held a cigar wrapped in rough, unfermented leaf, made in imitation of the way the ancient Maya bundled and smoked tobacco — the cigar to be smoked on 21 December 2012, 'the end of an era'. Founder Oscar Valladares originally did not smoke cigars at all: he was led into the industry while working as a travel-agency driver ferrying guests to the Rocky Patel factory, and his life story has itself come to embody the narrative character of the brand."
