      trivia: "In 1969 the banker and founder Jorge Bueso Arias brought seed back from Cuba and planted it in the Yarguera valley. This 'Yarguera tobacco' was exquisite in flavour but weak against blue mould, and was later crossed with the disease-resistant Criollo '98 to raise a hybrid preserving the character of the original strain. Besides its own marque, the factory also rolls H. Upmann Yarguera, which uses Yarguera-grown tobacco. In recent years the brand was driven to a temporary halt in shipments by the US sanctions surrounding Chen Zhi and its parent company, resuming only in May 2026 — a strangely eventful modern chapter quite unlike the usual lot of so venerable a house."
