      trivia: "La Invicta is a 'wartime cigar', born for a Britain cut off from Cuban leaf during the Second World War by US-dollar restrictions and the like; its name — 'the unvanquished' — carried a spirit undaunted by adversity. Hunters & Frankau, holder of the brand, claims a founding date of 1790, was involved in the launch of Montecristo, and in 1990 obtained the exclusive right to distribute all Havana brands in the United Kingdom. The Honduran version of La Invicta is rolled at the Plasencia-connected Tabacos de Oriente factory."
